romdev-core-bsnes
=================

wasm/bsnes_libretro.wasm and wasm/bsnes_libretro.js are built from bsnes
(https://github.com/libretro/bsnes, the libretro port of bsnes by byuu / Near
and contributors) at the commit pinned in romdevtools/scripts/versions.json
(cores.bsnes), with romdev's patches (romdevtools/scripts/patches/
bsnes-romdev.patch, bsnes-romdev-firmware.patch and patches/bsnes/).

bsnes is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
(GPL-3.0-only; the full text is GPLv3.txt in the bsnes source). libco and nall,
which bsnes includes, are under the ISC license. The built core is therefore
distributed under GPL-3.0; its corresponding source is the pinned bsnes commit
plus the romdev patch and build script named above.

No bsnes code is transplanted elsewhere in romdev: this core is the only
place bsnes runs. The firmware coprocessors that romdev's snes9x core and its
recompiled SNES carts run (the uPD96050 for the ST010/ST011, the ARM for the
ST018) are compiled from ares instead, which is ISC-licensed (see romdev's
NOTICE). The only file this build shares with that code is romdev's own
libco backend for WebAssembly (romdevtools/scripts/patches/libco-wasm/, MIT);
the chip state layout this core writes (patches/bsnes/romdev_bsnes_chipstate.h,
romdev's own, MIT) is matched field for field by the ares side's own header.

No coprocessor firmware, chip data ROM or boot ROM is included. The SPC700
boot ROM in this core is romdev's own clean-room reimplementation (romdevtools
scripts/spc700-ipl/ipl.asm, MIT), not the one bsnes embeds. The DSP-1 data
ROM, ST010 tables, Cx4 data ROM and Super Game Boy boot ROMs bsnes embeds are
emptied before it is built (patches/bsnes/strip-firmware.mjs); the chips'
firmware and the boot ROMs are not part of romdev, a user supplies them.
